hadiths[6]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17613","Hushaym narrated to us: Ya'la ibn 'Ata' narrated to us, who said: Jabir ibn Yazid ibn al-Aswad al-'Amiri narrated to me, from his father, who said: I was present with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at his Hajj. He said: I prayed with him the Fajr prayer in the mosque of al-Khayf, and when he finished his prayer, there were two men at the back of the mosque who had not prayed with him. He said: Bring them to me, so they were brought with their limbs trembling. He said: What prevented you from praying with us? They said: O Messenger of Allah, we had already prayed in our dwellings. He said: Do not do that; when you have prayed in your dwellings then come to a congregational mosque, pray with them, for it will be voluntary for you. My father said: And sometimes Hushaym was told: When he finished his prayer he moved aside, and he would say: He moved aside from his place."
"17614","'Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn 'Ata', from Jabir ibn Yazid ibn al-Aswad, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed Fajr at Mina, then turned aside and saw two men behind the people. He called for them, and they were brought with their limbs trembling. He said: What prevented you from praying with the people? They said: We had already prayed in our lodgings. He said: Do not do that; when one of you has prayed in his lodging then reaches the prayer with the imam, let him pray it with him, for it will be voluntary for him."
"17615","Bahz narrated to us: Abu 'Awanah narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn 'Ata', from Jabir ibn Yazid ibn al-Aswad, from his father, who said: We performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the Farewell Hajj. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in the Subh or Fajr prayer. He said: Then he turned aside, sitting, or faced the people with his face, and there were two men behind the people who had not prayed with the people. He said: Bring me these two men. He said: They were brought with their limbs trembling. He said: What prevented you from praying with the people? They said: O Messenger of Allah, we had already prayed in our lodgings. He said: Do not do that; when one of you has prayed in his lodging then reaches the prayer with the imam, let him pray it with him, for it will be voluntary for him. He said: One of them said: Ask forgiveness for me, O Messenger of Allah, so he asked forgiveness for him. He said: The people rose toward the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I rose with them, and I was on that day the strongest and most hardy of men. He said: I kept crowding through the people until I reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), took his hand and placed it either on my face or my chest. He said: I never found anything sweeter or cooler than the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: And he was on that day in the mosque of al-Khayf."
"17616","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us: Hisham ibn Hassan, Shu'bah, and Sharik informed us, from Ya'la ibn 'Ata', from Jabir ibn Yazid, from his father, who said: We prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the Fajr prayer in the mosque of al-Khayf, and he mentioned the hadith. He said: Sharik said in his hadith: One of them said: O Messenger of Allah, ask forgiveness for me. He said: May Allah forgive you."
"17617","Aswad ibn 'Amir and Abu al-Nadr said: Shu'bah narrated to us. Abu al-Nadr said: from Ya'la ibn 'Ata', and Aswad said: Ya'la ibn 'Ata' informed me, who said: I heard Jabir ibn Yazid ibn al-Aswad al-Suwa'i, from his father, that he prayed Subh with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he mentioned the hadith. He said: Then the people rose, taking his hand and wiping their faces with it. He said: I took his hand and wiped my face with it, and found it cooler than snow and sweeter in scent than musk."
"17618","Muhammad ibn Ja'far narrated to us: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn 'Ata', from Jabir ibn Yazid ibn al-Aswad, from his father, that he prayed the Subh prayer with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina, and he was a young lad. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had prayed, there were two men who had not prayed, so he called for them and they were brought with their limbs trembling. He said to them: What prevented you from praying with us? They said: We had prayed in our lodgings. He said: Do not do that; when you have prayed in your lodgings then reach the imam before he has prayed, pray with him, for it will be voluntary for you."
